5.1 Expanded 312-Reaction Mechanism

A comprehensive reaction mechanism is required to capture the coupled plasma chemistry of CO₂, O₂, H₂O, and trace VOCs at 600 Pa. The mechanism assembled for this work contains 312 reactions across five categories, summarized in Table 5.1. The full listing with rate coefficients is maintained in the archived simulation input files.

Table 5.1: Composition of the 312-Reaction Mechanism

Category Number of Reactions
Electron-impact (CO₂, O₂, H₂O) 52
Heavy-particle (O/OH/HO₂/H₂O₂/O₃/H) 104
VOC oxidation (HCHO, C₆H₆, NH₃) 61
Nitrogen species (NOₓ) 95
Total 312

Electron-impact cross-sections are drawn from the LXCat database: CO₂ (Phelps, updated 2025 compilation by Liu et al.), O₂ (Itikawa 2009), and H₂O (Itikawa 2005). Heavy-particle rate coefficients are sourced from the NIST Chemical Kinetics Database and the Kossyi et al. (1992) compilation for plasma environments. VOC oxidation pathways include hydrogen abstraction by O and OH, peroxy radical formation, and sequential oxidation to CO and CO₂. Nitrogen chemistry is included because the habitat atmosphere contains approximately 2.7% N₂, and NOₓ byproducts are regulated by SMAC limits.

Electron-impact rate coefficients are computed by convolution of the cross-section with the EEDF:

k_j(E/N, \mathbf{x}) = \sqrt{\frac{2e}{m_e}} \int_0^\infty \varepsilon \sigma_j(\varepsilon) f_0(\varepsilon; E/N, \mathbf{x}) \, d\varepsilon

where f_0 is obtained from BOLSIG+ solutions for the specific gas mixture and E/N.

