Analysis. The IPC configuration achieves higher initial VOC removal efficiency due to direct utilization of short-lived radicals (O, OH) and vibrationally excited species within the plasma zone. However, the deactivation rate is approximately three times higher than PPC. This is attributed to electron bombardment of the catalyst surface, which causes sputtering of active sites and accumulation of non-volatile carbonaceous deposits. The higher O₃ concentration in the PPC effluent is a consequence of O atom recombination in the afterglow; this is addressed by the downstream α-MnO₂ monolith (Section 6.4).

