6.5 Carbon Loop Closure with Moisture Management

Complete mineralization of VOCs produces CO as an intermediate and CO₂ as the final product. CO is a regulated contaminant (SMAC = 50 ppm), and its accumulation must be prevented. Hopcalite (CuMn₂O₄) is employed for CO oxidation to CO₂. However, Hopcalite is known to deactivate irreversibly in the presence of water vapor above approximately 0.5% relative humidity.

Theorem 6.1 (CO Oxidation Selectivity in CO₂ Background). Hopcalite maintains CO oxidation activity in high CO₂ backgrounds because CO and O₂ adsorb on different active sites than CO₂, which adsorbs weakly on surface oxygen vacancies.

Proof via Langmuir-Hinshelwood kinetics. The CO oxidation rate on Hopcalite follows:

r_{\text{CO}} = \frac{k K_{\text{CO}} P_{\text{CO}} K_{\text{O}_2}^{1/2} P_{\text{O}_2}^{1/2}}{(1 + K_{\text{CO}} P_{\text{CO}} + K_{\text{O}_2}^{1/2} P_{\text{O}_2}^{1/2} + K_{\text{CO}_2} P_{\text{CO}_2})^2}

Literature values (Lamb et al., 1922; Yoon et al., 2005) give K_{\text{CO}} \approx 0.5 Pa⁻¹, K_{\text{O}_2} \approx 0.1 Pa⁻¹, and K_{\text{CO}_2} \approx 0.002 Pa⁻¹. At Mars habitat conditions (P_{\text{CO}_2} \approx 300 Pa, P_{\text{CO}} \approx 5 Pa, P_{\text{O}_2} \approx 21 kPa), the CO₂ inhibition term K_{\text{CO}_2} P_{\text{CO}_2} \approx 0.6, compared to K_{\text{CO}} P_{\text{CO}} \approx 2.5. The rate reduction due to CO₂ is less than 20%, confirming that the carbon loop will not stall. ∎

Moisture Management Strategy. A silica gel guard bed (0.1 kg per person) is placed upstream of the Hopcalite bed to maintain relative humidity below 0.1%. The guard bed is regenerated during crew sleep periods (8 hours) using a 5 W heater, with desorbed water vented or condensed. As a fallback, Au/CeO₂ catalyst (insensitive to humidity up to 10% RH) is specified if Hopcalite deactivation is observed.

Carbon Loop Sequence. VOC → (DBD) → CO + CO₂ → (La₁.₇Cs₀.₃CoMnO₆) → partial CO oxidation → (Hopcalite) → complete CO oxidation to CO₂ → (MOF-74 or zeolite) → CO₂ capture for ISRU or venting.

