A.5 Theorem 3.5: Onsager Reciprocity Justification

Proof Sketch:

Entropy production at gas-solid interface:

\sigma = J_g \cdot \left(-\frac{\nabla \mu_g}{T}\right) + J_s \cdot \left(-\frac{\Delta G_s}{T}\right)

For heavy species near wall (T \approx 295 K), local equilibrium holds. Onsager relations give:

J_g = L_{11} X_g + L_{12} X_s, \quad J_s = L_{21} X_g + L_{22} X_s

with L_{12} = L_{21} by microscopic reversibility.

MD simulations (Zhang et al. 2024) for O atoms on perovskite: L_{12}/L_{11} \approx 0.12, indicating surface consumption alters near-wall concentration by up to 12%, justifying bidirectional coupling in the computational framework.

