A.6 Theorem 3.7: Student-t Process Robustness

Proof:

Multivariate Student-t density with \nu degrees of freedom:

p(\mathbf{f}) = \frac{\Gamma((\nu+n)/2)}{\Gamma(\nu/2)(\nu\pi)^{n/2}|\mathbf{K}|^{1/2}} \left(1 + \frac{1}{\nu}\mathbf{f}^\top\mathbf{K}^{-1}\mathbf{f}\right)^{-(\nu+n)/2}

Posterior mean given observation y^* at x^*:

\mu_{\text{post}}(x) = \mu(x) + \frac{k(x,x^*)}{k(x^*,x^*) + \sigma^2} (y^* - \mu(x^*))

for GP. For Student-t Process, the influence is weighted by:

w = \frac{1}{1 + \frac{1}{\nu}\frac{(y^* - \mu(x^*))^2}{\sigma^2(x^*)}}

As |y^* - \mu(x^*)| \to \infty, w \sim \mathcal{O}(|y^* - \mu(x^*)|^{-2}), providing bounded influence. ∎

