Appendix B — Core Chemistry Equations

B.1 Electron Energy Distribution Function (EEDF)

The two-term Boltzmann equation in energy space:

\frac{\partial}{\partial \varepsilon}\left( \frac{1}{3}\frac{eE^2}{N}\left[\sum_s x_s \sigma_m^s(\varepsilon)\right]^{-1} \varepsilon \frac{\partial f_0}{\partial \varepsilon} \right) + \sum_s N_s \sum_k \sigma_k^s(\varepsilon) \Delta\varepsilon_k f_0(\varepsilon) = 0

Normalization: \int_0^\infty \varepsilon^{1/2} f_0(\varepsilon) d\varepsilon = 1.

Electron temperature definition: T_e = \frac{2}{3} \langle \varepsilon \rangle = \frac{2}{3} \int_0^\infty \varepsilon^{3/2} f_0(\varepsilon) d\varepsilon.

B.2 Rate Equations for Species Concentrations

For species i in 0-D global model:

\frac{dn_i}{dt} = \sum_j k_j \prod_l n_l^{\nu_{lj}} - n_i \sum_m k_m \prod_l n_l^{\mu_{lm}} + S_i - L_i

where:

· k_j are rate coefficients (electron-impact from BOLSIG+, heavy-particle from Arrhenius)
· S_i = source from electron impact
· L_i = loss to walls: L_i = \frac{D_i}{\Lambda^2} n_i with diffusion length \Lambda = R/2.405 for cylindrical reactor.

B.3 Transport Equations (2-D Axisymmetric)

Drift-diffusion for neutral radicals:

\frac{\partial n_i}{\partial t} + \nabla\cdot(-D_i\nabla n_i + \mathbf{u} n_i) = S_i

For ions:

\frac{\partial n_i}{\partial t} + \nabla\cdot(-D_i\nabla n_i + \mathbf{u} n_i - z_i \mu_i n_i \mathbf{E}) = S_i

Boundary condition at catalyst surface:

-\mathbf{n}\cdot(-D_i\nabla n_i) = \frac{1}{4} \gamma_i v_{\text{th},i} n_i

where \gamma_i is the sticking coefficient.

B.4 Surface Reaction Kinetics (Mars-van Krevelen)

VOC oxidation on perovskite:

\text{VOC}_{(g)} + \text{O}_{\text{latt}} \rightarrow \text{CO}_x + \text{H}_2\text{O} + V_O^{••} + 2e'

\text{O}_{2(g)} + V_O^{••} + 2e' \rightarrow 2\text{O}_{\text{latt}}

Rate expression:

r = \frac{k_{\text{red}} P_{\text{VOC}} k_{\text{ox}} P_{\text{O}_2}^{1/2}}{k_{\text{red}} P_{\text{VOC}} + k_{\text{ox}} P_{\text{O}_2}^{1/2}}

