Appendix D — Control Algorithms and Surrogate Modeling

D.1 PCA Dimensionality Reduction

Input vector \mathbf{x} \in \mathbb{R}^{10}. Compute covariance matrix \Sigma = \frac{1}{n-1} \mathbf{X}^\top \mathbf{X} on standardized data. Eigenvalue decomposition: \Sigma = \mathbf{V} \boldsymbol{\Lambda} \mathbf{V}^\top. Retain first k=5 principal components capturing 95.7% variance. Transform: \mathbf{z} = \mathbf{V}_k^\top (\mathbf{x} - \boldsymbol{\mu}).

D.2 Student-t Process Surrogate

Prior:

f(\mathbf{z}) \sim \mathcal{TP}\left(\nu, 0, k(\mathbf{z}, \mathbf{z}')\right)

with Matérn-5/2 kernel:

k(\mathbf{z}, \mathbf{z}') = \sigma^2 \left(1 + \frac{\sqrt{5}r}{\ell} + \frac{5r^2}{3\ell^2}\right) \exp\left(-\frac{\sqrt{5}r}{\ell}\right), \quad r = \|\mathbf{z} - \mathbf{z}'\|

Posterior predictive distribution at test point \mathbf{z}_*:

p(f_* | \mathbf{y}) = \mathcal{T}\left(\nu + n, \mu_*, \frac{\nu + \beta - 2}{\nu + n - 2} \sigma_*^2\right)

where:

· \mu_* = \mathbf{k}_*^\top \mathbf{K}^{-1} \mathbf{y}
· \sigma_*^2 = k_{**} - \mathbf{k}_*^\top \mathbf{K}^{-1} \mathbf{k}_*
· \beta = \mathbf{y}^\top \mathbf{K}^{-1} \mathbf{y}

D.3 Soft Actor-Critic (SAC) Algorithm

Objective:

J(\pi) = \sum_t \mathbb{E}_{(s_t,a_t) \sim \rho_\pi} \left[ r(s_t,a_t) + \alpha \mathcal{H}(\pi(\cdot|s_t)) \right]

Actor Network: \pi_\phi(a|s) outputs Gaussian mean and log-std.

Critic Networks: Twin Q-networks Q_{\theta_1}, Q_{\theta_2} to reduce overestimation bias.

Loss Functions:

· Critic loss:
  L_Q(\theta) = \mathbb{E}_{(s,a,r,s',d) \sim \mathcal{D}} \left[ (Q_\theta(s,a) - y)^2 \right]
  where y = r + \gamma (1-d) \left( \min_{i=1,2} Q_{\bar{\theta}_i}(s',a') - \alpha \log \pi_\phi(a'|s') \right)
· Actor loss:
  L_\pi(\phi) = \mathbb{E}_{s \sim \mathcal{D}} \left[ \alpha \log \pi_\phi(a|s) - \min_{i=1,2} Q_{\theta_i}(s,a) \right]
· Temperature loss:
  L(\alpha) = \mathbb{E}_{s \sim \mathcal{D}} \left[ -\alpha \log \pi_\phi(a|s) - \alpha \bar{\mathcal{H}} \right]

D.4 Control Barrier Function (CBF) Safety Layer

Given nominal RL action u_{\text{RL}}, solve QP:

\begin{aligned}
\min_{u} & \quad \|u - u_{\text{RL}}\|^2 \\
\text{s.t.} & \quad L_f h_i(x) + L_g h_i(x) u + \alpha_i(h_i(x)) \ge 0, \quad i=1,2,3
\end{aligned}

where h_i are barrier functions:

· h_1(x) = 0.05 - [\text{O}_3]
· h_2(x) = \text{stability\_index} - 0.7
· h_3(x) = 50 - [\text{CO}]

Class-\mathcal{K} functions \alpha_i(h) = \gamma_i h with \gamma_i > 0.

D.5 Control Lyapunov-Barrier Function (CLBF) Construction

Proposed CLBF:

V(x) = (x - x_{\text{goal}})^\top P (x - x_{\text{goal}}) + \sum_{i=1}^3 \frac{c_i}{h_i(x)} \cdot \mathbb{1}_{h_i(x) < \epsilon}

where P \succ 0 solves Lyapunov equation for linearized dynamics, and c_i > 0 are barrier weights. The condition \inf_u \dot{V} \le -\alpha_3 V ensures simultaneous stabilization and safety.

D.6 Domain Randomization for Sim-to-Real Transfer

During offline training, parameters are sampled:

· Catalyst deactivation rate: \mathcal{U}(0.85 \times \text{nominal}, 1.15 \times \text{nominal})
· Dust loading: \mathcal{U}(0, 2\times \text{baseline})
· Humidity: \mathcal{U}(1\%, 3\%)
· Sensor noise: \mathcal{N}(0, 0.02^2)
· Outlier probability: 5% with magnitude \mathcal{U}(3\sigma, 10\sigma)

