---------------------------------------------------------
Input: Training data (Z_train, y_train), kernel type (Matérn-5/2),
       degrees of freedom ν (e.g., 4)
Output: Optimized hyperparameters θ = {σ², ℓ, ν}

1. Define negative log marginal likelihood (NLML):
   NLML(θ) = -log p(y|Z,θ)
   = 0.5 log|K| + ((ν+n)/2) log(1 + (1/ν) y^T K^{-1} y) + const

2. Initialize hyperparameters:
   σ² = Var(y_train)
   ℓ = median pairwise distance in Z_train
   ν = 4

3. Optimize NLML using L-BFGS-B:
   While not converged:
      Compute K with current θ
      Compute K^{-1} (Cholesky)
      Compute gradient ∂NLML/∂θ
      Update θ

4. Return θ*
```

