F.10 Algorithm: Catalyst Regeneration Control Logic

Purpose: Determine when to trigger thermal regeneration and manage the process.

```
Algorithm 10: Regeneration Control
---------------------------------------------------------
Input: Cumulative VOC throughput C_VOC, current catalyst activity A,
       crew schedule (sleep period indicator)
Output: Regeneration command (True/False), heater setpoint

1. Estimate current activity from surrogate:
   A = f_deactivation(C_VOC, operating_hours)

2. If A < 0.8 and sleep_period == True:
   a. Set regeneration_mode = True
   b. Set heater_setpoint = 400 K
   c. Set DBD power = 20% nominal (reduced to limit O₃)
   d. Start 2-hour timer

3. During regeneration:
   Monitor [O₃] via CBF layer (ensures <0.05 ppm)
   If [O₃] > 0.04 ppm:
      Reduce DBD power further

4. After 2 hours:
   Set regeneration_mode = False
   Set heater_setpoint = 295 K
   Set DBD power = nominal (from RL policy)
   Reset cumulative VOC throughput counter

5. Return regeneration_mode, heater_setpoint
```

